* verify-fold.bp - the BASIC half of gplbld/verify-fold.py.  Plan section M1;
* the intent is the port's gplbld/verify-fold.ps1 section 4.
*
* IT IS STAGED, COMPILED AND RUN BY verify-fold.py IN THE CALLER'S OWN ACCOUNT.
* It is an ordinary program - NOT $internal - so it compiles as an unprivileged
* user with no developer build.
*
* WHY A PROGRAM AT ALL: no verb reaches this lookup.  A verb folds the name it
* was typed with before it opens anything, so the BASIC OPEN statement - which
* goes through _VOC_REF and nothing else - can only be measured from BASIC.  A
* hard-coded literal such as open "$SAVEDLISTS" is exactly that case.
*
* ***EVERY ANSWER IS PRINTED AS "TAG=value" ON ITS OWN LINE, AND EACH TAG IS
* PRINTED ON EXACTLY ONE PATH PER VALUE.***  Y is printed only from the THEN of
* the open, N only from its ELSE, so a fault part way leaves the tag absent
* rather than looking like an answer.
*
* ***IT LEAVES ITS Q-POINTER BEHIND ON PURPOSE*** so verify-fold.py can read it
* back in a fresh session before removing it.
*
program zzfold

   crt 'ZZFOLD.BEGIN=1'

   open 'VOC' to voc.f else
      crt 'ZZFOLD.FATAL=cannot open VOC'
      stop
   end

* The Q-pointer fixture: a lower-case VOC id whose TARGET is named in upper
* case.  The target's real VOC id is lower (verify-fold.py made it with
* CREATE.FILE), so only the fold on the Q-pointer target can resolve it.
   write 'Q':@fm:'':@fm:'ZZFOLDF' to voc.f, 'zzfoldq'
   crt 'Q.WRITTEN=1'

* CONTROL: the name exactly as its VOC id is spelled.  Opens before and after.
   open 'zzfoldf' to f1 then crt 'OPEN.EXACT=Y' else crt 'OPEN.EXACT=N'

* THE ROW: a lower-case VOC id opened by its upper-case name.  N before the
* fold, Y after.
   open 'ZZFOLDF' to f2 then crt 'OPEN.UPPER=Y' else crt 'OPEN.UPPER=N'

* THE UPWARD HALF: an upper-case VOC id opened by its lower-case name.
   open 'voc' to f3 then crt 'OPEN.VOCLOWER=Y' else crt 'OPEN.VOCLOWER=N'

* CONTROL: a name in the VOC in no case at all.  N before and after, so the
* fold has not turned into "every open succeeds".
   open 'ZZFOLDNONE' to f4 then crt 'OPEN.ABSENT=Y' else crt 'OPEN.ABSENT=N'

* The Q-pointer's target.
   open 'zzfoldq' to f5 then crt 'OPEN.QTARGET=Y' else crt 'OPEN.QTARGET=N'

   crt 'ZZFOLD.END=1'
end
